{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 10, :comments ["<b>Your name is Jacob; your name shall no longer be called Jacob.</b> Alone — for two names shall be yours, Jacob and Israel. For if 'your name is Jacob' were uprooted entirely, they would say: it was because of עקבה (supplanting) that your name was called Jacob, as it is written: ״הכי קרא שמו יעקב ויעקבני זה פעמים״ (Therefore was his name called Jacob, and he has supplanted me these two times). But they shall call your name at times thus and at times thus. Whereas with Abraham it was not said 'your name [shall no longer be called] Abram'; therefore one who calls Abraham [by the name] Abram transgresses a positive commandment." "<b>But Israel shall be your name.</b> An expression of dominion, as it is written: ״כי שרית עם אלקים״ (for you have struggled with Elohim). This name befits you, for kings shall come forth from your loins. Here Rashi explained: this is Saul and Ish-bosheth. And if you ask: what is this that we learned, 'Why was Avner punished? Because he delayed the monarchy of the house of David two and a half years, by crowning Ish-bosheth son of Saul' — what reason is there for him to be punished for this, was it not a decree of Scripture, as Rashi explained? One may answer: he was punished because his intention was to shame David by delaying his monarchy."], :book :genesis, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 35, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:07:26.756000320Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}